# Root .dockerignore for repo-root build contexts (PDI-2523).
#
# All standard-product images build with `-f <product>/Dockerfile .` so the
# product Dockerfiles can COPY runtime/common/, runtime/pingdata/ and
# legal/license.txt from the build context. With the whole repo as
# context, exclusions here are the supply-chain surface: everything not
# needed by a build must be out.
#
# Build inputs that DO go to the daemon: <product>/Dockerfile,
# <product>/opt/, <product>/tmp/ (bits override), <product>/keys.gpg,
# runtime/common/, runtime/pingdata/, legal/license.txt,
# ldap-sdk-tools/wait-for, pingdelegator/nginx.conf.

# Secrets and local env — never enter the build cache/layers.
.env
**/.env
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
# Tracked exception: delegator's DH params are a deliberate build input
# (COPYied via pingdelegator/opt; build.sh.pre unconditionally enables
# ssl_dhparam pointing at it) — without this negation **/*.pem silently
# drops it from the context and the shipped image cannot start nginx.
!pingdelegator/opt/staging/instance/etc/certs/dhparam.pem

# VCS and CI internals.
.git
.gitlab-ci.yml
.github
.claude
.polaris
.playwright*

# Local scratch, editor and OS droppings.
scratch/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp

# Docs and tests never reach a build (the runtime server README must
# stay: it is COPYied into images as /opt/server/README.md and hook
# 06-copy-product-bits.sh copies /opt/server/* at startup; legal/
# license.txt needs no negation — nothing excludes .txt).
helm-tests
**/tests/
**/versions.json
**/*.md
!runtime/common/server/README.md

# Shared-configs submodule (release-note tooling only).
shared-configs

# Non-product directories (nothing in a product build copies from these).
ci_scripts

# Product tmp/ dirs are NOT excluded: they are build inputs — local
# product.zip bits overrides for get-product-bits.sh, copied via
# COPY ["<product>/tmp/", "/tmp/"]. Per-product .gitignore files already
# keep actual zips out of git; untracked local zips stay a local-only risk.
